In `parseProjectSymlinks`, the inner loop processes multiline symlink items starting from `index + 1`. However, the outer loop's `index` variable is never updated to skip these processed lines. As a result, the outer loop will redundantly re-evaluate every list item line.

To avoid redundant processing and potential parsing bugs, we should declare `itemIndex` outside the inner loop and update `index` to `itemIndex - 1` after the inner loop completes.

```javascript
    const symlinks = [];
    let itemIndex = index + 1;
    for (; itemIndex < lines.length; itemIndex += 1) {
      const itemLine = lines[itemIndex];
      if (itemLine.trim() === '' || itemLine.trimStart().startsWith('#')) continue;
      if (leadingSpaces(itemLine) <= indent) break;

      const itemMatch = /^ {6}-\s+(.+?)\s*$/.exec(itemLine);
      if (!itemMatch) continue;
      symlinks.push(parseScalar(itemMatch[1]));
    }
    projects.set(currentProject, symlinks);
    index = itemIndex - 1;
